Package: rewindr
Title: Time-Travel Debugging for Data Pipelines
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Bernard Isekah", "Osangir", , "b.osangir@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Neudata Consulting Ltd", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
  )
Description: Records the data after every step of a pipeline or script and
    finds the step where it silently went wrong. Native and 'magrittr' pipes
    are split into stages, scripts run statement by statement in a sandbox,
    and in-place edits become new versions of an object. Consecutive states
    are compared for lost or duplicated rows, new missing values, type
    changes and changed cells, and joins are checked for unmatched keys,
    keys that differ only in whitespace or case, and duplicated lookup keys
    that multiply rows. A 'shiny' app scrubs backward and forward through
    every state. Fixes can be suggested from built-in rules or requested
    from the 'Claude' API, re-run in a sandbox and compared with the
    original, and a script can be turned into a 'Docker' recipe with pinned
    package versions. Developed by Neudata Consulting Ltd.
